    <item>
      <title>Reverse a linked list (Iterative way)</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/linkedlist/lesson6/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/linkedlist/lesson6/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Here is the link to the problem: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eB1G2QtcOyM&amp;amp;list=PLk6CEY9XxSICJ0XSI7fbQFiEpDHISJxqT&amp;amp;index=6&#34;&gt;Reverse a linked list (Iterative way)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;problem-statement-with-thought-process&#34;&gt;Problem Statement with Thought Process:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To reverse a linked list iteratively, we can use three pointers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Previous Pointer&lt;/strong&gt;: Keeps track of the previous node, which will help us reverse the links.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current Pointer&lt;/strong&gt;: Points to the current node we’re processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next Pointer&lt;/strong&gt;: Temporarily stores the next node before we change the &lt;code&gt;current&lt;/code&gt; node&amp;rsquo;s link.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
